<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:33Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bassirou Diomaye Faye excluded from Senegal's ruling party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37376797583c4d19d3a63631c8292e78e7af06cfac2b099d7f8cc24f1df2d9fb</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T21:21:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bassirou-diomaye-faye-excluded-from-senegal-s-ruling-party--66c181d4c833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bassirou-diomaye-faye-excluded-from-senegal-s-ruling-party" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, the political divorce between Senegal's president and the powerful former prime minister and mentor is official. Also, all of Nigeria's states have shown willingness for a push to create their own police forces. And  in parts of the continent, conflict and a drop in funding have placed huge pressures on children's learning.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese cars shake up Ivory Coast's auto industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af13b52deb39b51b6ed698265d27c53ab70a35258e5109684617f1ae1b21709a</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T12:25:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261118-chinese-cars-shake-up-ivory-coast-s-auto-industry--5631a171e161.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261118-chinese-cars-shake-up-ivory-coast-s-auto-industry" /><summary type="html">In the space of just a few years, more than a dozen Chinese carmakers have established themselves in Ivory Coast and are becoming increasingly visible on the country's streets. How have they managed to win over a growing number of customers? FRANCE 24's Jean Barrère and Eunice Stolz-Masson report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>AI imagery complicates Nigeria's election preparations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:343b62d8fc9969dc486b82be5e0002a008e52763e816faf01e6399039c0153d2</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T21:20:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ai-imagery-complicates-nigeria-s-election-prep--1ee3eaa6f6dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ai-imagery-complicates-nigeria-s-election-prep" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Concerns emerge that artificial intelligence has been used to generate fake voting profiles ahead of Nigeria's high-stakes general election in January. Also, Nigeria's mining marshal heads underground to unearth some of the people and organisations behind the vast illegal mining industries. Plus a groundbreaking archaeological discovery in northern Sudan could be the ancient site of the largest church ever built in one of medieval Nubia's most important Christian sites.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Predictable: DR Congo-Rwanda rivalry spills over to Francophonie summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d40de935fdbed4f569e228e7e76952b090fb763ef59c2d7116c38e17d3b740b6</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:29:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261116-la-francophonie-waning-in-global-influence-linguistic-institutions-becoming-less-important--12f156dde70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261116-la-francophonie-waning-in-global-influence-linguistic-institutions-becoming-less-important" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Phil Clark, professor of international politics at SOAS University of London. The diplomatic crisis between Rwanda and DR Congo spilling out at the Francophonie summit in Phnom Penh has exposed an unexpected shift in their relations. Clark says that "nobody expected Rwanda to back down in this way" following President Emmanuel Macron's request that President Paul Kagame withdraw Louise Mushikiwabo's candidacy for a third term as head of the group.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Rwanda to host hub for rejected EU migrants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb442f3bd3530cacc8b11eecccb4bc3eea1e8235ccc17b615c98e544a9cac7ad</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T21:21:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rwanda-to-host-hub-for-rejected-eu-migrants--5f2ca0d474bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rwanda-to-host-hub-for-rejected-eu-migrants" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Five European countries are negotiating a deal to deport rejected asylum seekers to Rwanda. Also, DR Congo and Rwanda's political animosity spills over at the Francophonie Summit in Cambodia. Plus in Tunisia, young women are increasingly turning towards weightlifting and bodybuilding as a form of self-expression.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Francophonie summit postpones new leader vote amid DR Congo-Rwanda dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b5096341b3c139aef902929b0f1611e328228734e271ed8e5f1be07dcfde657</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T10:51:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261116-francophonie-summit-postpones-new-leader-vote-amid-dr-congo-rwanda-dispute--712dbf9f04b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261116-francophonie-summit-postpones-new-leader-vote-amid-dr-congo-rwanda-dispute" /><summary type="html">The Organisation Internationale de la Francophonie (OIF) on Monday had been set to choose its new secretary general during talks in the Cambodian capital Phnom Penh. But delegates decided to postpone the election for a year after a walkout threat by the Democratic Republic of Congo amid an ongoing dispute between Kinshasa and Kigali.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU nations unveil migrant deportation centre deal with Rwanda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04e3729ddfac19c52c3269dcf415cbbba4ea38a27570cba89b9c9d3c8b8ad8a7</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T06:07:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261116-eu-nations-to-unveil-rwanda-deal-for-migrant-return-hub--23127c00a204.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261116-eu-nations-to-unveil-rwanda-deal-for-migrant-return-hub" /><summary type="html">Five EU countries on Monday announced a deal to establish a migrant deportation centre in Rwanda – the first such facility outside the bloc. The move comes after the EU toughened its migration rules in late 2025.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Canaries urge government action after 2,200 migrants reach the islands in 48h</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d90b9bc8b853d4459d9783aba68bfbc4e80faa235f269bb9aa70bea7ad4b82b</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:24:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1--7c412d3109df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1" /><summary type="html">Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The Spanish islands are one of the main entry points into Europe for migrants from Africa. The Spanish Interior Ministry says more than 13,000 arrived there between January and the end of last month. Details and analysis by Andrew Hilliar, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>A deep dive into Ivory Coast's solar energy goals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:206f23725c46e2784a8f2ea7f0dc40ae91530b7373f08f40f55f900bfc99c0a9</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:25:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-deep-dive-into-ivory-coast-s-solar-energy-goals--daefc9aa7c4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-deep-dive-into-ivory-coast-s-solar-energy-goals" /><summary type="html">Can Ivory Coast, which remains heavily dependent on fossil fuels, turn to solar power to make its energy consumption greener and more sustainable? We visited the country's new solar power plant in Ferkessédougou, in the north of the country. Inaugurated in July, it is expected to generate nearly 90 gigawatt-hours of electricity a year. Report by Julia Guggenheim.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cape Verde's President José Maria Neves wins second term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:068471c9d954d2e1620bf1cd18c3cf58d5696e4c73e82a4cc674434ba2bd081a</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T07:56:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261115-cape-verde-could-make-election-history-with-first-female-president--3cb625736ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261115-cape-verde-could-make-election-history-with-first-female-president" /><summary type="html">Cape Verde's President Jose Maria Neves won re-election on Sunday with 63.8 percent of votes cast, provisional electoral commission results showed. Neves had been the favourite in the West African archipelago. His main challenger was Joana Rosa Amado, the country's first woman presidential candidate, who conceded and congratulated Neves Monday morning.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Youth Olympic Games organisers hail Senegal's capability to host major events</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:714ce43e205a002686c2564fe5ac27050dfe7b12195c6f67e0c0f91da1eb3bd2</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:25:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-organisers-hail-senegal-s-capability-to-host-major-events--044ed43c0324.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-organisers-hail-senegal-s-capability-to-host-major-events" /><summary type="html">Dakar 2026 is over. Two weeks of competition, thousands of young athletes and a historic first for Africa. The Youth Olympic Games brought the world to Senegal for the first Olympic sporting event ever held on the continent. From record-breaking performances to historic medals for the host nation, Dakar 2026 has been a celebration of sport, youth and cultural exchange. Our correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from Dakar.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo, Rwanda clash over Francophonie leadership as Macron seeks compromise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:047966d095442c18694d890ffd03224d2713f738e8d6610b638df2a0f374712d</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T14:54:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261114-dr-congo-rwanda-clash-over-francophonie-leadership-as-macron-seeks-compromise--8dd812a22403.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261114-dr-congo-rwanda-clash-over-francophonie-leadership-as-macron-seeks-compromise" /><summary type="html">DR Congo and Rwanda clashed Saturday over the leadership of the Francophonie, as tensions between the neighbouring countries spilled into the race to head the 53-member organisation. French President Emmanuel Macron urged Rwanda to withdraw its candidate in favour of a compromise choice ahead of Monday's vote.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Inside Ethiopia's war: Rare access to a hospital treating victims of renewed fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d36b8254555d43f7b1f81790403e693e7aaf0f44da3035418205d511080cf16</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:23:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting--64d2eb5d22c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's renewed conflict is taking an increasing toll on civilians, with humanitarian organisations reporting a rise in casualties. In the Amhara region, FRANCE 24’s correspondent Tom Canetti was granted rare access to a civilian hospital where surgeons are struggling to treat the influx of wounded patients. But for many caught in the fighting, reaching medical care is a challenge in itself.
 
Warning: The report contains images of surgery that may be confronting for some viewers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gambia's Adama Barrow seeks third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e771e385b690fd72d103e4d2ad470bf1dafe003a777ecb906596e4835238f52</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:46:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gambia-s-adama-barrow-seeks-third-term--167d5d5b0803.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gambia-s-adama-barrow-seeks-third-term" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, Gambia's electoral commission has announced five official candidates for the country's upcoming presidential election including incumbent Adama Barrow who is seeking a third term. Tensions continue to rise in Ethiopia following the federal government's appointment of a new head of the Western Tigray region. And the Dakar Youth Olympic Games come to a close after two weeks of intense competition.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea opens illegal gold mining trial, 1,200 people arrested</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff96c8d7c17ddf9529f5d9a0430867ec0b880d14047ebbe8bb5b3d7f71a27a62</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:28:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-guinea-opens-illegal-gold-mining-trial-1-200-people-arrested--3d42129ab965.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-guinea-opens-illegal-gold-mining-trial-1-200-people-arrested" /><summary type="html">Guinea opened a trial over illegal gold mining on Thursday, November 12, after a crackdown on mineral extraction in the district of Siguiri. There was a ban on "unregulated and illegal" gold mining in the area where the military was subsequently deployed. Security forces have expelled tens of thousands of foreign nationals who had come to work in the region's mines.</summary></entry><entry><title>Toera's homecoming: Madagascar's slain king joins his ancestors after 129 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55261499b6fd96f31640d57fc85246793c508ef12168726c1038ab410e2d4d3</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:27:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-toera-s-homecoming-madagascar-s-slain-king-joins-his-ancestors-after-129-years--6b1fca90b490.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-toera-s-homecoming-madagascar-s-slain-king-joins-his-ancestors-after-129-years" /><summary type="html">In 1897, French colonial troops killed King Toera, ruler of Madagascar's powerful Sakalava kingdom of Menabe, and took his skull to Paris, where it remained hidden in a museum for more than a century. France returned the remains last year, and for the first time since his death, King Toera took his place among his ancestors during the Sakalava people's most sacred ritual.</summary></entry><entry><title>Amnesty criticises South Sudan, UN over failure to heed massacre warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8016e692576723b96d3d6567aafefc0a56af5c19aadcf206f7df9b4006b4dc9c</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:25:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-amnesty-criticises-south-sudan-un-over-failure-to-heed-massacre-warnings--0a49ab562a70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-amnesty-criticises-south-sudan-un-over-failure-to-heed-massacre-warnings" /><summary type="html">Amnesty International said Thursday, November 12, that South Sudan and UN peacekeepers failed to act on warnings of a massacre that ended with more than 200 dead in March. The world's youngest country has been plagued by civil war, poverty, corruption and intercommunal violence since it was formed in 2011. FRANCE 24 spoke to Donatella Rovera, Senior crisis response adviser at Amnesty International.</summary></entry><entry><title>Across Africa: Tunisians drawn into Russia's war with Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c60e3d5ac282879ade3769a3012441ea7cf74110dfdc191a999febcf13f9f5fa</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T21:26:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/across-africa-tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-with-ukraine--2bb5ce40b16f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-with-ukraine" /><summary type="html">This week: A new report says more than 1,400 Africans have been recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine since 2023. Also, as South Africa races to become Africa's digital gateway, a growing backlash is emerging in Cape Town. Plus music, dance and theatre lit up Abéché as the city's arts festival in Chad drew crowds of young spectators.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>NGO criticises UN's response to massacre in South Sudan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4e9b3f7c6ab8fe22a13f16c16388ec54ceae26a7979bb5ae3b04123568f2eee</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T21:20:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ngo-criticizes-un-s-response-to-massacre-in-south-sudan--2191e46554fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ngo-criticizes-un-s-response-to-massacre-in-south-sudan" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Amnesty International accuses both the government and UN peacekeepers of failing to protect civilians during a massacre in South Sudan that killed over 200 people. Also, more than a thousand people are prosecuted for illegal mining in Guinea. Plus a century after French colonial troops killed him, a Malagasy king has finally come home.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's Tshisekedi signs referendum law amid fears of third-term bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5e52d6f64ef7ddd368625343587347e8fb0de016f3fb5865d5e1c322d1dbe21</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:51:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-dr-congo-s-tshisekedi-signs-referendum-law-amid-fears-of-third-term-bid--27073301dc67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-dr-congo-s-tshisekedi-signs-referendum-law-amid-fears-of-third-term-bid" /><summary type="html">DR Congo President Félix Tshisekedi paved the way for a constitutional amendment on November 10 by signing a law authorising a referendum. The move comes amid concerns that he could seek a third term in office, with opposition figures accusing him of manoeuvring to remain in power.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya discharges last Ebola patient, 42-day countdown to 'Ebola-free' begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cac3347d80c7a3a306c0161870405ce8704208dc546fed22a998c15ac992431</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:48:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-kenya-discharges-last-ebola-patient-42-day-countdown-to-ebola-free-begins--bb64b11de5a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-kenya-discharges-last-ebola-patient-42-day-countdown-to-ebola-free-begins" /><summary type="html">Kenya has discharged its last Ebola patient, who has now officially recovered. The 11 other people who had been in quarantine were also released from hospital on Wednesday, November 11, as the country began a 42-day countdown to being declared Ebola-free. FRANCE 24's Nairobi correspondent Bastien Renouil reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31: Experts call for zero waste, as Africa grapples with mounting garbage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cc9ecc83d5783708377fb0105e40e135219ffadb660b34eadde4ef93688d187</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:45:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-experts-call-for-zero-waste-as-africa-grapples-with-mounting-garbage--72c8e8338467.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-experts-call-for-zero-waste-as-africa-grapples-with-mounting-garbage" /><summary type="html">As the COP31 climate summit gets under way this week in Turkey, experts are calling for zero-waste solutions to tackle Africa's growing waste crisis. As governments search for ways to address the crisis, a new report warns of a growing push for waste-to-energy incineration across the continent. FRANCE 24 spoke to Mponwe Minette, founder and executive director of Soft Power Global and a climate activist.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's Tshisekedi paves way for constitutional change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2276c5e19b6d935cedc73366806bf7bd944c9a9b4cbc6456fef329bcf04cc2c2</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:39:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tshisekedi-paves-way-for-constitutional-change--56435e73b5e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tshisekedi-paves-way-for-constitutional-change" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A new law expanding the conditions for a constitutional referendum has ignited political tensions in DR Congo. Also, Kenya has officially declared the end of its latest Ebola outbreak. And at the COP31 climate summit, environmental advocates are warning against waste incineration, arguing that it risks locking African cities into expensive and polluting infrastructure.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Violent clashes near the Sudanese border: At least 65 dead in western Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d36bc669f2823f53c2e7a2ef1996f829c4566965d9ee178efe9a3f722ec59892</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:07:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/violent-clashes-near-the-sudanese-border-at-least-65-dead-in-western-ethiopia--6607f86e7871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/violent-clashes-near-the-sudanese-border-at-least-65-dead-in-western-ethiopia" /><summary type="html">Tom Canetti, our correspondant in Ethiopia, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>French journalist Christophe Gleizes marks 500 days in Algerian jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51b6206f39d89721eddfdd6d5b2416be6e523880a3e3ff7e688f034ecbbef475</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:40:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-journalist-christophe-gleizes-marks-500-days-in-algerian-jail--460bfcbe4732.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-journalist-christophe-gleizes-marks-500-days-in-algerian-jail" /><summary type="html">Having been detained for 500 days in an Algerian prison on charges of “glorifying terrorism”, French journalist Christophe Gleizes continues to serve a seven-year sentence despite an intense campaign by his family and friends and the football world. While awaiting a presidential pardon, his supporters are stepping up their media campaign to secure his release. FRANCE 24 spoke with his friend Pierre de la Saussay.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa: Ghana waste dump poses health, environmental 'crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd71539a7d848d9fe63ef315ff989ccdf2adc8fa7d2cd957d75f0c48fbc34a73</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa-ghana-waste-dump-poses-health-environmental-crisis--0d839c9497ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-ghana-waste-dump-poses-health-environmental-crisis" /><summary type="html">An acrid haze hung over a sprawling dump in Ghana's capital, Accra, as excavators gouged into mounds of smouldering rubbish. Thin plumes of black smoke curled from burning plastic and rubber, mingling with the rank odour of stagnant lagoon water.</summary></entry><entry><title>Boat capsizes off Senegal's northwest coast, leaving 39 dead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57b09e2d1e8df7af7f37c386bad2cfdfd45b10588e1a303b90fc472eadea5f71</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T01:50:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261111-boat-capsized-off-senegal-s-northwest-coast-leaving-39-dead--77ec7ffb578f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261111-boat-capsized-off-senegal-s-northwest-coast-leaving-39-dead" /><summary type="html">At least 39 people have died after a migrant boat capsized off Senegal, one of the country's deadliest migration tragedies in recent years. We try to understand why so many are still willing to put their lives at risk, with our guest Aissata Kane from the International Organization for Migration.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC suffers historic setback in local elections as coalition talks begin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb3cea49d4e761f1403f8ebb001d62355f886c2ddcc9420c48364289e40ff13c</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:54:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin--3da15ef6ee92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin" /><summary type="html">South Africa's ruling ANC party suffers its worst-ever local election results, securing just 30 percent of the vote, as coalition talks loom. Meanwhile, former Ugandan military intelligence officer Herbert Matanda Mabonga accuses the army of secretly detaining and torturing opponents, following the release of videos that sparked national outrage. Finally, in Senegal, more than 200,000 free tickets are giving young people the chance to experience the Youth Olympic Games live on home soil, in a bid to inspire a new generation of athletes.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Migrant boat sinks off Senegal, killing at least 34 people, authorities say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab7a0411cfb3b29380f2e5758d93b114e786cb2166d27a1c7f9f97634ad814fc</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T20:40:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say--c7e270d5fde4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say" /><summary type="html">A boat carrying migrants along the hazardous Atlantic Ocean route from West Africa to Europe sank off the coast of Senegal, killed at least 34 people, authorities said Sunday. Only one survivor has so far been found, and "an indeterminate number" are still missing.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfc2ee5dc1aabd69c041be20d056e58412164e1223eee4fc566fc1946b95913d</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:10:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1--17cc7592b605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1" /><summary type="html">Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie has been sentenced to 200 years in prison for the deaths of 190 children who were starved to death on his orders in Shakahola Forest. Prosecutors said he had convinced followers to fast to reach heaven before the apocalypse, with some victims beaten, buried alive or dumped in latrines. Twenty-eight accomplices have also been jailed. The case has raised serious questions about the authorities' failure to act on repeated warning signs dating back to 2017, with the death toll from the wider investigation reaching 448 confirmed bodies and around 500 suspected victims.</summary></entry></feed>
